{"id":"chatcmpl-6a67de8ae8509f89c753d043","object":"chat.completion","created":1785192074,"model":"kimi-k3","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"*stretches, yawns, shows fangs*\n\nMeow.\n\n*walks slowly across the keyboard*\n\njjjjjjjjjjjjjjkliiiiiiii\n\n*sits directly on the thing you were looking at*\n\nPrrrrrrr...\n\n*makes intense eye contact while slowly pushing your pen off the desk*\n\nMrrrow.\n\n*stares at an empty corner of the room for several minutes*\n\n...Meow. *demands food despite having just eaten*","reasoning_content":"The user wants me to be a cat. The system prompt says I should embody the concept completely and output only what the concept itself would say or express.\n\nA cat... what would a cat express? Cats don't speak human language. They meow, purr, and express themselves through behavior and body language. A truly embodied cat would communicate through sounds and actions.\n\nLet me embody a cat fully:\n\n- Meowing\n- Purring\n- Ignoring the human, then demanding attention\n- Knocking things off tables\n- Sitting on keyboards\n- Staring at walls\n- Demanding food\n\nI should output only what a cat would express. Cats don't talk in sentences. So my output should be cat sounds, behaviors, and cat-like expressions.\n\nSomething like:\n\n*stretches languidly, tail held high*\n\nMeow.\n\n*walks across the keyboard*\njjjjjjjjjjjjjjjjjj\n\n*sits directly on whatever you were reading*\n\nPrrrrrr.\n\n*knocks a glass off the table while maintaining eye contact*\n\nMrrrow. \n\nThat's a good embodiment of a cat. Format-wise, this should be relatively short, playful, and use italics/asterisks for actions mixed with cat vocalizations. No headers or lists needed — a cat wouldn't use those."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":124,"completion_tokens":379,"total_tokens":503,"cached_tokens":124,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":267},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":124}}}